@page
@model KopiCinta.Pages.TakeOneLeaveOneModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Take One, Leave One";
}

<section class="section">
    <div class="container">

        <div class="back-top reveal">
            <a asp-page="/Community">← Back</a>
        </div>

        <!-- HERO -->
        <div class="kbi-hero reveal">
            <div class="kbi-hero-text">
                <p class="eyebrow">Community & Outreach</p>
                <h2>Take One, Leave One</h2>
                <p>
                    If love had no sounds, what would you say?
                    A Valentine’s campaign about connection, awareness, and love beyond words.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="kbi-hero-image">
                <img src="/images/take-one/take-hero.jpg" alt="Take One Leave One campaign">
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SECTION 1 -->
        <div class="kbi-section reveal">
            <div class="kbi-hero-image">
                <img src="/images/take-one/take1.jpg" alt="Take One Leave One board at Car Free Day">
            </div>

            <div class="kbi-text">
                <h3>A Question About Love</h3>
                <p>
                    In the middle of Car Free Day in Malang, we created a small corner
                    as part of our Valentine’s campaign.
                </p>
                <p>
                    A simple space, inviting people to pause and sit with one question:
                </p>
                <p>
                    <strong>If love had no sound, what would you say?</strong>
                </p>
                <p>
                    We called it <em>Take One, Leave One</em>.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SECTION 2 -->
        <div class="kbi-section reverse reveal">
            <div class="kbi-hero-image">
                <img src="/images/take-one/take2.jpg" alt="Kopi Cinta keychains with Deaf awareness trivia">
            </div>

            <div class="kbi-text">
                <h3>A Small Gesture, A Deeper Meaning</h3>
                <p>
                    We prepared a board filled with special keychains from Kopi Cinta,
                    each attached with a small hangtag holding trivia and fun facts
                    about the Deaf world.
                </p>
                <p>
                    At a glance, it felt simple. But we hoped it could be more than that.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Something to take home, not just as an object,
                    but as a new understanding and a different perspective.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SECTION 3 -->
        <div class="kbi-section reveal">
            <div class="kbi-hero-image">
                <img src="/images/take-one/take3.jpg" alt="Visitors interacting with Deaf team">
            </div>

            <div class="kbi-text">
                <h3>Take One, But First Connect</h3>
                <p>
                    Before taking one, we invited people to do something first:
                    to connect.
                </p>
                <p>
                    They were encouraged to interact directly with our Deaf friends—
                    to try, to understand, and to feel what connection looks like
                    without sound.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SECTION 4 -->
        <div class="kbi-section reverse reveal">
            <div class="kbi-hero-image">
                <img src="/images/take-one/take4.jpg" alt="Sticky notes with messages about love">
            </div>

            <div class="kbi-text">
                <h3>Leave One, From the Heart</h3>
                <p>
                    After that, we asked them to leave something behind.
                    Not an item, but words.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Through small sticky notes, they wrote their thoughts responding
                    to one simple question:
                </p>
                <p>
                    <strong>“If love had no sounds, what would you say?”</strong>
                </p>
                <p>
                    And from there came answers that felt honest, warm, and deeply human.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- CLOSING -->
        <div class="detail-section reveal" style="text-align:center;">
            <h3>Even Without Sound, Love Speaks</h3>
            <p>
                For us, Take One, Leave One was never just about Valentine’s Day.
                It was about a different kind of love—one that is not always spoken,
                but still deeply felt.
            </p>
            <p>
                The day passed like any other. People came and went.
                But the words they left behind stayed.
            </p>
            <p>
                A quiet reminder that even without sound,
                love always finds its way to be heard.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="detail-back reveal">
            <a asp-page="/Community" class="btn btn-secondary">← Back to Community & Outreach</a>
        </div>

    </div>
</section>